# The Bellic tab: a party member's fighting profile, for the protagonist and for a companion.
#
# Information only, so the assertions are on text: the four stat sections, a source organ beside a
# number, a skill expanded into the terms behind its dice, and the same screen for a beast — whose
# body has no hands to hold a weapon and whose skills are fangs and claws rather than fists.
#
# --fill-party at a heart of 1 gives one companion, a beast. --grant-mm brawling makes the hands'
# first skill known, so a row reads as ready and its breakdown names a modus mentis.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --fill-party --grant-mm brawling:2 --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --period noon

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 45

# --- the protagonist -----------------------------------------------------------------
manage Bellic
wait 1
expect B E L L I C
expect TURN
expect ESCAPE AND RECOVERY
expect STRIKING
expect DEFENCE
expect Cinetic points
expect backbone
expect Natural defence
expect lower limbs
expect SKILLS
expect Right hand
expect Punch
dump

manage Bellic Punch
wait 1
expect PUNCH
expect Where the dice come from
expect brawling
expect natural attack
expect against the target's defence
dump

# --- the companion: a beast ----------------------------------------------------------
manage member 1
wait 1
expect beast anatomy
expect Natural defence
expect legs
expect Fangs
expect-not Right hand
expect no hand to hold one with
dump

quit
